Kind: ablation
Issue: #723
Takes out: nothing -- a probe: thread_select() gives a bound thread four quanta where it gave one, so preempt_test's three threads, bound to one processor, change hands a quarter as often as a quantum of min_quantum ticks promises. Before #723 the test counted nothing, and passed it.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 5 300 -smp 4
Expect: preempt_test: WRONG .* changed hands [0-9]+ times in [0-9]+ ticks
Note: entry 5 is -P at four processors, the form whose three threads run on an application processor, watched from the boot processor. 723-quantum-every-tick asks the other side, at one processor on entry 21.

